The audit found 2 load-bearing issues. The exact report was printed to stdout, but `findings-building.md` could not be created because the workspace is read-only and approvals are disabled.

`A Metric Must Measure the Work, Not the Question` passed all five checks, including reciprocal parentage and its future, well-formed countdown.

# Building family audit — findings
VERDICT: FINDINGS
COUNT: 2
## Findings
1. Constitutional Traceability — No Unconstitutional Work — its semantic LLM ship gate explicitly fails open when the reviewer is degraded or unreachable, while *No Silent Degradation to Brittle Fallback* requires any gating LLM call that suffers provider failure to swap providers or fail closed — a reader cannot determine whether a reviewer outage must halt shipment or permit an unjudged weak fit, because obeying either article violates the other.
2. Conservative Outbound: Act, Don't Notify — its practice section says nothing checks a new emitter's default at build time, but its Applied-through section simultaneously claims a lint that flags newly enabled proactive emitters lacking a human-needs-it justification — the registry gives opposite accounts of whether this obligation has a build-time enforcement surface, so a reader cannot tell whether silent-by-default is mechanically checked or only review guidance.
